        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 67-year-old female patient, admitted on 14/04/2017 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, physical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without pneumonic consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypercapnic respiratory failure. Blood tests and pulse oximetry were performed to monitor her condition. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Clinical response was satisfactory, with improvement in oxygen saturation and symptom relief. She was discharged on 15/04/2017 in stable condition. Please continue inhaled maintenance therapy and ensure follow-up spirometry. Smoking cessation counselling and pulmonary rehabilitation referral are recommended. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician], Department of Internal Medicine.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
